---
layout: null
permalink: /search.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The docs site search index (task 120).

  GitHub Pages only runs allowlisted plugins, so the index is built here in
  Liquid at build time and scored in the browser by assets/js/search.js — no
  gem, no service, no build step outside Jekyll. One record per section: the
  rendered HTML of each page is split on its heading anchors, so a hit can link
  to "#vincent-task-list" instead of dumping the reader at the top of a
  120 KB reference page.

  Record keys are short because every byte ships to the reader:
  p = page title, t = section title, u = link, x = searchable text.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign raw_open = '{' | append: '% raw %' | append: '}' -%}
{%- assign raw_close = '{' | append: '% endraw %' | append: '}' -%}
{%- assign sep = '' -%}
[
{%- for p in site.html_pages -%}
  {%- if p.search == false or p.sitemap == false -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign page_url = p.url | relative_url -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Pages escape their Go-template examples for Liquid; markdownify does not run
    Liquid, so the raw markers would otherwise land in the index as text.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign source = p.content | replace: raw_open, '' | replace: raw_close, '' -%}
  {%- assign rendered = source | markdownify -%}
  {%- assign flat = rendered | replace: '<h3 id="', '<h2 id="' | replace: '<h4 id="', '<h2 id="' | replace: '<h5 id="', '<h2 id="' | replace: '<h6 id="', '<h2 id="' -%}
  {%- assign chunks = flat | split: '<h2 id="' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    jekyll-titles-from-headings finds no heading on a page that opens with a raw
    tag, so those pages would be indexed under their filename. The rendered h1
    is the page's own title in every case.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign page_title = p.title -%}
  {%- unless page_title -%}
    {%- assign h1_parts = rendered | split: '<h1' -%}
    {%- if h1_parts.size > 1 -%}
      {%- assign page_title = h1_parts[1] | split: '</h1>' | first | split: '">' | last | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
  {%- comment -%}The home page leads with a logo and has no heading at all.{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign page_title = page_title | default: site.title | strip -%}
  {%- for chunk in chunks -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}
      {%- assign heading = page_title -%}
      {%- assign link = page_url -%}
      {%- assign body = chunk -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign anchor = chunk | split: '">' | first -%}
      {%- assign body = chunk | remove_first: anchor | remove_first: '">' -%}
      {%- if anchor contains ' ' or anchor contains '<' -%}
        {%- comment -%}A heading carrying extra attributes: index it without a deep link.{%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign link = page_url -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign link = page_url | append: '#' | append: anchor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign heading = body | split: '</h' | first | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign text = body | strip_html | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&' | normalize_whitespace | strip -%}
    {%- if heading == '' and text == '' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {{ sep }}{"p":{{ page_title | jsonify }},"t":{{ heading | jsonify }},"u":{{ link | jsonify }},"x":{{ text | jsonify }}}
    {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
